phase 1 progress and setup

devices:-
at first we used 2 Cisco ISR4331 Routers Models and 4 Switches and 12 PCs as shown in the topology.png then the PCs were distributed across the Four LANs

WAN serial links:-
to establish the serial link we need to install the NIM-2T module into the expansion slot on the two Routers to enable the serial link connection WAN
and then we connected the two Routers using the serial DTE cable Serial 0/1/0 interface

after that we configured the gigabit interfaces on the Routers to serve as gateways for the LANs and assigned the IPs on the 4 LANs

on Router 1:
gig0/0/0 LAN1: 172.16.10.1/24
gig0/0/1 LAN2: 172.16.20.1/24

on Router 2:
gig0/0/0 LAN3: 172.16.30.1/24
gig0/0/1 LAN4: 172.16.40.1/24



then i configured the ip addresses on serial 0/1/0 and enabled the serial cable for the Routers on the CLI by using these comannds:-

on Router1:
interface s0/1/0
ip add 10.10.10.1 255.255.255.252
no sh

on Router2:
interface s0/1/0
ip add 10.10.10.2 255.255.255.252
no sh

after that we configuerd all the PCs with there static IPs and subnet maskes and their Default gateways

